{"content":[{"c":["GENTLENESS"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["In the OT an attitude of humility or bending low (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.22.36","r":"2Sam.22.36","rawR":"2Sam.22.36","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.22.36","value":"2Sam.22.36"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 22:36"},", ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"; cf. ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.18.35","r":"Ps.18.35","rawR":"Ps.18.35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.18.35","value":"Ps.18.35"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 18:35"},", ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). Its adjectival and adverbial forms (“gentle,” “gently”) can mean courteous and unpretentious (",{"href":"?bref=Pr.15.4","r":"Pr.15.4","rawR":"Pr.15.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Pr.15.4","value":"Pr.15.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Prv 15:4"},"), quiet and tender (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.32.2","r":"Deut.32.2","rawR":"Deut.32.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.32.2","value":"Deut.32.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 32:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.8.6","r":"Isa.8.6","rawR":"Isa.8.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.8.6","value":"Isa.8.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 8:6"},"), or unharsh (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.18.5","r":"2Sam.18.5","rawR":"2Sam.18.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.18.5","value":"2Sam.18.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 18:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.15.11","r":"Job.15.11","rawR":"Job.15.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.15.11","value":"Job.15.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 15:11"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["In the NT several words are translated “gentleness,” “gentle,” or “gently.” Shades of meaning include (1) mildness, meekness, forbearance (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.11.29","r":"Matt.11.29","rawR":"Matt.11.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.11.29","value":"Matt.11.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 11:29"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Cor.4.21","r":"1Cor.4.21","rawR":"1Cor.4.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Cor.4.21","value":"1Cor.4.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Cor 4:21"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Cor.10.1","r":"2Cor.10.1","rawR":"2Cor.10.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Cor.10.1","value":"2Cor.10.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Cor 10:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Gal.5.23","r":"Gal.5.23","rawR":"Gal.5.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gal.5.23","value":"Gal.5.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gal 5:23"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Tim.6.11","r":"1Tim.6.11","rawR":"1Tim.6.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Tim.6.11","value":"1Tim.6.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Tm 6:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Pet.3.4,15","r":"1Pet.3.4,15","rawR":"1Pet.3.4,15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Pet.3.4,15","value":"1Pet.3.4,15"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Pt 3:4, 15"},"), or a courteous and unassuming attitude (",{"href":"?bref=2Tim.2.25","r":"2Tim.2.25","rawR":"2Tim.2.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Tim.2.25","value":"2Tim.2.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Tm 2:25"},"); (2) kindness expressed toward others (",{"href":"?bref=1Thes.2.7","r":"1Thes.2.7","rawR":"1Thes.2.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Thes.2.7","value":"1Thes.2.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Thes 2:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Tim.2.24","r":"2Tim.2.24","rawR":"2Tim.2.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Tim.2.24","value":"2Tim.2.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Tm 2:24"},", ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"); and (3) fitting, fair, or seemly (",{"href":"?bref=1Tim.3.3","r":"1Tim.3.3","rawR":"1Tim.3.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Tim.3.3","value":"1Tim.3.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Tm 3:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Titus.3.2","r":"Titus.3.2","rawR":"Titus.3.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Titus.3.2","value":"Titus.3.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ti 3:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Pet.2.18","r":"1Pet.2.18","rawR":"1Pet.2.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Pet.2.18","value":"1Pet.2.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Pt 2:18"},"). Church leaders and other believers are instructed to deal gently with those who stumble (",{"href":"?bref=Gal.6.1","r":"Gal.6.1","rawR":"Gal.6.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gal.6.1","value":"Gal.6.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gal 6:1"},"), oppose the faith (",{"href":"?bref=2Tim.2.25","r":"2Tim.2.25","rawR":"2Tim.2.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Tim.2.25","value":"2Tim.2.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Tm 2:25"},"), or are ignorant and wayward (",{"href":"?bref=Heb.5.2","r":"Heb.5.2","rawR":"Heb.5.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Heb.5.2","value":"Heb.5.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Heb 5:2"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Gentleness","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Sm 22:36","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.22.36","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.22.36","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.22.36"},{"anchorText":"Ps 18:35","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.18.35","rawQueryValue":"Ps.18.35","sourceRefExact":"Ps.18.35"},{"anchorText":"Prv 15:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Pr.15.4","rawQueryValue":"Pr.15.4","sourceRefExact":"Pr.15.4"},{"anchorText":"Dt 32:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.32.2","rawQueryValue":"Deut.32.2","sourceRefExact":"Deut.32.2"},{"anchorText":"Is 8:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.8.6","rawQueryValue":"Isa.8.6","sourceRefExact":"Isa.8.6"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 18:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.18.5","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.18.5","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.18.5"},{"anchorText":"Jb 15:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.15.11","rawQueryValue":"Job.15.11","sourceRefExact":"Job.15.11"},{"anchorText":"Mt 11:29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.11.29","rawQueryValue":"Matt.11.29","sourceRefExact":"Matt.11.29"},{"anchorText":"1 Cor 4:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Cor.4.21","rawQueryValue":"1Cor.4.21","sourceRefExact":"1Cor.4.21"},{"anchorText":"2 Cor 10:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Cor.10.1","rawQueryValue":"2Cor.10.1","sourceRefExact